ome back  against very strongly Caroline Flint  formal Abram who lost her seat in don  valley said this i don't believe anybody  who has been the architects of our  european policy in the last few years is  credible to be leader and then she went  on to say kirsten led us down the path  of a second referendum and i'm afraid  emily Thornbury did as well she said to  one of my colleagues I'm glad my  constituents aren't as stupid as yours  now you've come back saying that's not  true you're pursuing legal action well I  can't I mean you can see in the hands of  my lawyers I mean I've issued a letter  for action and you know I would need  that along with everything else I need  to do next week I need to see my  solicitors and we need signature it so I  mean there's a you know you can't just  maybe not rubbish about me and not  expect me to take legal action I mean  I'm always I mean people can slag me off  and they do but so long as they do it on  the basis of truth  take it on the chin but if you start  making things up I have to take legal  action and I have done  I'm afraid on three or four previous  occasions and when newspapers have said  things about me that aren't true and  when my political opponents have said  things about me that aren't true and it  looks like I may have to do it again how  about the even though she's a Labour MP  which is no I I deeply regret that we're  going to need to do this but if we have  to do it we have to do how about the  wider point that people like yourselves  and KO samet should not lead the Labour  Party because she backed a second  referendum well I think that I think  that we shouldn't have had a general  election on a single issue I think that  what we did that we gave Boris Johnson  power by allowing him to wrap himself up  in the lie that he could get brexit done  by the end of January because it won't  be done we will need to continue to  negotiate a relationship with Europe and  what obviously we will be leaving at the  